            <ArticleTitle>Fatal myocardial infarction in hypertrophic cardiomyopathy associated with non-penetrating chest trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>317-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial infarction as a result of injury to the coronary arteries is a rare complication of non-penetrating chest trauma. We report a case of fatal inferior wall myocardial infarction following traumatic injury to the right coronary artery, complicated by atrioventricular dissociation, in a patient with a combination of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and non-occlusive coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
